SELECT 'Guide', f.id, $kb106$guide-families$kb106$, $kb107$Families — group clients into households$kb107$, $kb108$Map clients into a family, see combined AUM and give the household one RM.$kb108$, $kb109$A family groups related clients so you can see the household's combined position and review them together.

![Families](shot:1)

## Create a family

1. Open **Clients → Families** and click **New family**.
2. Choose the **head** of the family. The name follows the firm's pattern (for example "Sharma Family") and can be edited; the family code (FAM-0001…) is automatic.
3. Add notes if you wish and save. The family's RM, branch, category and review schedule come from the head's client record.

![New family](shot:2)

## Map clients

- The **Unmapped clients** card shows how many clients belong to no family; click **Map clients** to add them.
- Open a family to add or remove members and set each member's relationship.
- Members take the head's relationship manager and address, and the family's review frequency.

## Tidy up

- **Merge duplicates** combines families created twice.
- **Family settings** sets the relationship types and the defaults for new families.
- The category tiles (All, Super HNI, HNI, Upper Middle, Middle) filter the list.$kb109$, $kb110$[{"storageKey":"/kb/families.jpg","caption":"The Families list with combined AUM, SIP and review dates.","alt":"The Families list with combined AUM, SIP and review dates."},{"storageKey":"/kb/families-new.jpg","caption":"New family: pick the head and the notes — the rest fills from the head.","alt":"New family: pick the head and the notes — the rest fills from the head."}]$kb110$::jsonb, 3, true, now(), 9
