SELECT 'Guide', f.id, $kb286$guide-campaigns$kb286$, $kb287$Marketing campaigns$kb287$, $kb288$Log webinars, seminars and ad bursts, or schedule a broadcast, and see leads and conversions per campaign.$kb288$, $kb289$Campaigns tie your marketing effort to the leads and clients it brings.

![Campaigns](shot:1)

## Create a campaign

1. Open **Marketing Campaigns** and click **New campaign**.
2. Choose the **Campaign type** — **WhatsApp**, **Email** or **Webinar / Seminar** — and give it a **Campaign name** and a **Theme / hook** (for example Tax Saving, SIP Power, NFO Launch, Diwali).
3. Set the **Start date** and **End date**, and describe the **Target audience** for your records.
4. For a broadcast, open **Broadcast send (optional)**: choose an approved **Template**, then the **Audience** — **All clients**, **All leads**, **By criteria** or **Specific clients** — and click **Set audience**. Recipients without a valid contact or consent are skipped automatically and audited.
5. Leave **Schedule** blank to send right after launch, or pick a date and time, and set the **Throttle (per min)**.
6. Save. Campaigns can need approval; **Pending approval** counts them.

![New campaign](shot:2)

## Measure

The tiles show **Active** campaigns and, year to date, **Leads**, **Meetings**, **Conversions** and **Spend**. The **Conversion report** shows which campaigns converted. Use **Export** to download the list.$kb289$, $kb290$[{"storageKey":"/kb/campaigns.jpg","caption":"Marketing Campaigns: active campaigns, leads, meetings, conversions and spend.","alt":"Marketing Campaigns: active campaigns, leads, meetings, conversions and spend."},{"storageKey":"/kb/campaign-new.jpg","caption":"New campaign.","alt":"New campaign."}]$kb290$::jsonb, 3, true, now(), 39
