INSERT INTO kb_articles (series, folder_id, slug, title, hook, solution_md, screenshots, read_minutes, published, published_at, sort_order)
SELECT 'Guide', f.id, $kb292$guide-communications$kb292$, $kb293$Communications — every message, one timeline$kb293$, $kb294$Compose a message, see what was sent, delivered, read or failed, and review client responses.$kb294$, $kb295$Communications is the log of every WhatsApp, email and SMS the CRM has sent.

![Communications](shot:1)

## Send a message

1. Open **Settings → Communications** and click **Compose**. The **Compose email** page opens.
2. Choose the **Recipient**: **Client** (search by name, PAN or mobile) or **Email address**.
3. Write the **Subject** and the **Message**. Use {{name}} for the client's name — the MF risk disclaimer and your ARN signature are appended automatically.
4. Choose the **Category** (for example Transactional (service)), tick **Schedule for later** if you want a later time, and click **Send now**. The message passes the consent and compliance checks first; if it is blocked, the log shows why.

![Compose](shot:2)

## Follow what happened

- The tiles count **Scheduled**, **Sent**, **Delivered**, **Read** and **Failed** messages.
- The list shows recipient, subject, status and time; search by recipient, subject or template, and star a message to keep it.
- **Client responses** opens what clients replied; **Cadence (SOP)** shows the firm's contact cadence.

## The rules every send follows

An opt-out always blocks a message. Marketing messages need a recorded consent. Service and transactional messages go out unless the client has opted out. WhatsApp marketing also needs an open session window.$kb295$, $kb296$[{"storageKey":"/kb/communications.jpg","caption":"Communications with Scheduled, Sent, Delivered, Read and Failed counts.","alt":"Communications with Scheduled, Sent, Delivered, Read and Failed counts."},{"storageKey":"/kb/compose.jpg","caption":"Compose: recipient, channel, template and message.","alt":"Compose: recipient, channel, template and message."}]$kb296$::jsonb, 3, true, now(), 40
